      "quote": "The typical Australian... was seldom religious in the sense in which the word is generally used.",
      "attribution": "C.E.W. Bean",
      "source": "The Australian Imperial Force, 1921",
      "description": "Australia is one of the most secular nations on earth, deeply suspicious of \"wowsers\" (moralizers), \"Bible-bashers,\" and anyone claiming a monopoly on truth. The skepticism extends to politicians, bosses, and grand ideologies, creating a culture where \"Bullshit Detection\" is a primary survival skill.",
      "establishes": "This establishes Skepticism as the Filter. It is the immune system against dogma, rejecting high-flown rhetoric in favor of \"the pub test.\" The Australian mind is empirical and cynical; it trusts what it can see and touch, and mocks what it cannot. This rejects \"Big Ideas\" in favor of \"What Works,\" making the nation difficult to radicalize but also difficult to inspire purely on vision. It grounds the values in the tangible reality of the here-and-now, refusing to mortgage the present for a utopian future. It represents the triumph of the profane over the sacred.",
