      "establishes": "This establishes Luck as the Fuel. It acknowledges that the wealth is often dug up, not invented, creating a unique economic drive. It acts as a \"Resource Curse\" that breeds complacency (\"She'll be right\") but also provides the \"Social Dividend\" that funds the Fair Go. It questions whether the success is earned or gifted, creating a subtle anxiety about the stability of the luck. It implies the drive is passive rather than active. It empowers the \"Miner\" over the \"Maker.\"",
