        "note": "Kanon Role — The Engine (υ = +0.5, ψ = +0.7 · Good): This establishes Speculation as the Engine. The Gold Rush embedded a gambler's mentality at the heart of Australian economics and soul. Unlike the Puritan work ethic (Work = Virtue), the goldfields preached Luck + Effort = Fortune. Carboni's vision of the Southern Cross as \"refuge for all the oppressed\" planted the seed of multicultural potential that would take a century to germinate. The rush democratized wealth, severing the link between class and capital and creating the \"Digger\" archetype—neither lord nor serf, but a free man with a shovel and a dream. It reinforces the national obsession with property, mining shares, and the belief that the \"Big Win\" waits just around the corner."
