      "description": "Section 245 of the Electoral Act introduced compulsory voting, a rare feature in world democracies, reflecting the belief that customized participation was essential for legitimacy. It turned the franchise from a \"Right\" to be exercised at will into a \"Duty\" to be performed under penalty of law. It codified the idea that the state has a claim on the political attention of every adult citizen.",
