      "uid": "3.6.5",
      "addr": "Where.Cause.How",
      "plane": 3,
      "senseId": "3.6",
      "name": "The Opencut",
      "cleanName": "The Opencut",
      "role": "Method",
      "fn": false,
      "quote": "An immense scar on the face of the earth... visible from space.",
      "attribution": "Popular Description",
      "source": "Kalgoorlie Super Pit",
      "description": "The Fimiston Open Pit (Super Pit) is a hole so vast it consumes the horizon, a negative monument to Australian industry. It represents the industrial method of extracting the \"Lode\" where the earth is not \"worked\" but removed entirely. It is the inverse of the mountain, a cathedral of emptiness.",
      "establishes": "This establishes Excavation as the Method. The primary interaction with the \"Foundation\" is to remove it. We do not \"farm\" the rock; we export it. It defines the \"How\" of the economy as a massive earth-moving operation. It symbolizes a culture that is willing to turn the landscape inside out to get at the value.",
      "coreMeaning": "The primary interaction with the \"Foundation\" is to remove it. We do not \"farm\" the rock; we export it.",
      "coords": {
        "v": -0.2,
        "psi": 0.7
      },
      "zone": "Greatest Lie",
      "rationale": "Extraction (+ψ) with environmental cost (-υ).",
      "hansonVerdict": "HIT",
      "alboVerdict": null,
      "inHanson353": true,
      "qA": "We should see through and reject the national flaw of The Opencut (Method) (the primary interaction with the \"Foundation\" is to remove it. We do not \"farm\" the rock; we export it).",
      "qB": "In my own everyday actions, I refuse to practise or excuse The Opencut even when it would be convenient.",
      "qC": "People in my everyday circle see through The Opencut and refuse to practise or excuse it.",
      "qD": "Across Australia today, our wider society and institutions actually resist and overcome The Opencut rather than being captured by it.",
      "help": {
        "highA": "You see through and reject The Opencut (Method)—recognising how it distorts or betrays the Australian ethos (The primary interaction with the \"Foundation\" is to remove it. We do not \"farm\" the rock; we export it.).",
        "lowA": "You accept, excuse, or do not see a problem with The Opencut, allowing its extractive or divisive logic to stand.",
        "highB": "In your daily life and community, people are free from The Opencut and actively resist its pull.",
        "lowB": "Your community, workplace, or political reality is still trapped in or harmed by The Opencut.",
        "note": "⚠️ Corrective / Shadow Node (υ = -0.2, ψ = 0.7): Because The Opencut is a negative shadow or failure mode in the Australian Kanon, the rating scale is framed in the restorative direction—rating +1 to +5 means rejecting and overcoming the shadow (Kanon HIT), while rating −1 to −5 means being captured by it (Kanon FAIL). This establishes Excavation as the Method. The primary interaction with the \"Foundation\" is to remove it. We do not \"farm\" the rock; we export it. It defines the \"How\" of the economy as a massive earth-moving operation. It symbolizes a culture that is willing to turn the landscape inside out to get at the value."
      },
