      "name": "The Impact",
      "cleanName": "The Impact",
      "role": "Origin",
      "fn": false,
      "quote": "The risk to Earth would no longer be a matter of chance.",
      "attribution": "Eugene Shoemaker",
      "source": "Context of Comet/Asteroid Research, 1997",
      "description": "The Australian landscape preserves ancient \"Star Wounds\" like the Acraman Crater because the shield is so stable. Discovered by Williams and confirmed by Shoemaker, these craters remind us that the \"Cause\" of the geography is partly extraterrestrial. The land bears the scars of deep time collisions that elsewhere have been erased by erosion.",
      "establishes": "This establishes Violence as the Origin. The land suggests that the tranquility of the bush masks a violent history. It aligns the \"Cause\" of the land with the random, catastrophic nature of the universe. It creates a \"Landscape of Memory\" where every feature tells a story of impact and survival.",
