      "source": "The Tyranny of Distance, 1966",
      "description": "Blainey observed that the vast majority of Australians live in a boomerang-shaped arc on the south-east coast. We cling to the edge of the continent, looking outwards to the sea rather than inwards to the \"Red Heart.\" The \"Where\" of the result is a thin green crescent of civilization surrounding a vast, empty core.",
