      "name": "The Future",
      "cleanName": "The Future",
      "role": "Destiny",
      "fn": false,
      "quote": "You see, psychologically, Australia must understand it has to live in the region around it. Australia must find its security in Asia; it cannot find its security from Asia.",
      "attribution": "Paul Keating",
      "source": "Foreign Policy Speech, 1994",
      "description": "Keating articulated the final \"Effect\" of our location: we are a western nation permanently anchored in the Asian hemisphere. Our future depends on reconciling our \"History\" (British) with our \"Geography\" (Asian). We cannot remain a fortress forever; we must engage.",
      "establishes": "This establishes Integration as the Destiny. The \"Result\" of the land's location is an inevitable hybridization. We are the \"South Land\" of Asia. This vector prompts the nation to evolve from a \"Colonial Outpost\" to a \"Regional Power.\" It defines the future as the end of the \"Tyranny of Distance\" and the beginning of the \"Opportunity of Proximity.\"",
