      "description": "The \"Right to a Holiday\" is a non-negotiable object of Australian life. Whether it is \"The Shack\" on the coast or the \"Trip Overseas,\" the Holiday is the reward for the \"Year's Slog.\" It is a period of \"suspended responsibility\" where the rules of the normal world are relaxed. It is the ritual acknowledgment that the environment is for enjoyment, not just production.",
