      "source": "",
      "description": "The Strike is the historical tool of the \"Collective,\" deeply embedded in the national psyche since the Shearers' Strike of 1891. It operates on the axiom \"One out, all out,\" meaning that an injury to one is an injury to all. It weaponizes the withdrawal of labor to force the employer to acknowledge the human value of the worker, functioning as the primary lever of the \"Battler.\"",
