      "description": "The economic collapses (1890s, 1930s) scarred the national psyche with the \"Spirit of the Susso\" (Sustenance) and the \"Wallaby Track\"—the itinerant search for work. They ingrained a profound fear of poverty and a distrust of banks that lasted for generations, driving the obsession with \"Security\" and \"Home Ownership.\" The trauma proved that prosperity was fragile.",
