      "quote": "United we stand, divided we fall.",
      "attribution": "",
      "source": "Eight Hour Day Banner, 1856",
      "description": "The Unionist is the \"Collective Agent,\" the person who derives power from membership in a larger body rather than individual excellence. Australia was the laboratory of the \"Workingman's Paradise,\" where the method of advancement was not \"Individual Ambition\" (USA) but \"Collective Bargaining\" (Australia). The \"Ticket\" (Union Membership) was the license to work on major worksites; without it, you were a \"Scab\" excluded from the job.",
      "establishes": "This establishes The Unionist as the Operator. It defines the Australian method of solving inequality: \"Combination,\" meaning the pooling of weak individual voices into a single powerful demand. The \"Who\" in Australia operates best in a \"Mob\" or a \"Rank,\" not as a lone hero. It institutionalized the \"Strike\" as a legitimate tool of negotiation, not just a desperate rebellion. The Unionist method created the 8-Hour Day (1856), the Living Wage (1907), and the compulsory arbitration system—the infrastructure of the Fair Go.",
