      "attribution": "",
      "source": "David McBride, (Afghan Files Whistleblower, 2019)",
      "description": "The Whistleblower is the \"Loyal Traitor\"—the only agent in the Australian method permitted to break the sacred code of \"Mateship\" in service of a higher, abstract \"Truth.\" David McBride provides the precise operational distinction that justifies this breach: the soldier's oath is to the \"Country\" (The Ideal), not the \"Government\" (The Boss), creating a necessary separation between the Nation and the State.",
      "establishes": "This establishes The Whistleblower as the Safety Valve of Mateship. In a culture that values loyalty above all else, the system would become a closed loop of corruption without this specific vector of betrayal. The Whistleblower is not a \"Rat\" in the criminal sense, but a \"Correction Mechanism\" that resets the system when the \"Government of the Day\" violates the core definition of the \"Country.\" It proves that the Australian Method places the integrity of the \"Public Right to Know\" above the hierarchy of command, but only when the stakes are existential.",
