      "description": "The Umpire is the secular god of the Australian method, a figure of absolute authority accepted by a naturally anti-authoritarian people. We accept the \"Final Verdict\" of the Tribunal—even when we hate it—because our cultural psyche was trained by the Laws of Cricket long before it was trained by the Constitution, viewing the raised finger as an absolute termination of debate.",
      "establishes": "This establishes The Umpire as the Civilizer of Conflict. Justice Higgins applied this sporting logic to the nation itself, viewing the industrial landscape not as a free market, but as a \"Province\" that must be conquered by Law, just as the land was conquered by the plough. The Umpire exists to remove the violence from the struggle between Capital and Labor, turning a \"Street Fight\" into a \"Court Ruling\" and ensuring the game continues, proving that Australians prefer a \"Fair Ruling\" by an authority over a \"Free Fight\" in the wild.",
