      "description": "In 1907, Justice Higgins ruled that the owner of the Harvester Factory must pay a wage sufficient for a worker to support a family \"in frugal comfort\"—the first \"Living Wage\" decision in the world. The \"Test Case\" became the tool of economic distribution, replacing the chaos of industrial warfare with the order of a courtroom. Instead of a market riot, we have a \"Hearing\"; instead of a strike, we have a precedent.",
