      "description": "The Mallee scrub of South Australia was considered impossible to farm because the hidden roots would smash any standard plough. Richard and Clarence Smith invented a plough with hinged blades that \"jumped\" over the obstacles rather than fighting them—allowing the blade to ride up over a stump and drop back down without breaking. This simple innovation opened millions of acres of previously useless land to agriculture.",
