      "source": "Settlers and Convicts, 1847",
      "description": "This proverb, recorded in the early shearing sheds, upended the class structure of the Old World. In Britain, the \"Master\" was better by definition of birth. In Australia, the only measure that mattered was output—the tally on the board. The Ringer (champion shearer) was the King of the Shed, regardless of his parentage.",
