      "description": "Distance is the \"Mother\" of the Australian method, the silent dictator of our history. Geoffrey Blainey's thesis argues that the sheer mileage between nodes dictated every choice: from the gauge of the railways to the invention of the Pedal Radio, the terrifying realization that \"No help is coming\" forced the colony to abandon the \"Cargo Cult\" mentality and adopt the \"Maker\" mentality.",
