      "description": "The Meeting (Inquiry) is the Australian method of \"Processing Trauma.\" When a crisis hits, we do not panic and we do not revolt; we form a Commission to create a formal, safe space for the unheard to speak into the official record, turning trauma into bureaucracy and rage into recommendations.",
      "establishes": "This establishes The Meeting as the Dampener of Voltage. While noble in intent, it is often used as the \"Graveyard of Urgency\"—a mechanism to slow down history and talk an issue to death. The Meeting is a tool of social stability, used to manage the \"heat\" of a crisis until the public anger subsides. It proves that the Australian method prefers \"Process\" over \"Action,\" believing that if we talk about a problem long enough, it has technically been dealt with.",
