      "role": "Dispossession",
      "fn": false,
      "quote": "I have the honour to inform your Lordship that I have this day taken possession of this territory in the Name of His Majesty King George the Third.",
      "attribution": "Captain James Cook",
      "source": "Journal Entry, Possession Island, Torres Strait, 22 August 1770",
      "description": "Cook planted the flag at the northernmost point of the east coast after sailing the length of Australia, claiming a continent with a written entry and a raised standard. Cook claimed the land under the legal fiction of Terra Nullius—that the land was empty and therefore belonged to no one. This fiction deliberately ignored 65,000 years of Indigenous habitation, erasing an entire civilization with a piece of paper. The \"What\" of the foundation is an Act of Erasure, claiming ownership of something that was never unowned.",
