      "description": "Macquarie, the \"Father of Australia,\" recognized that a sustainable society required voluntary migrants with skills and capital, not merely transported felons. Macquarie saw that a nation cannot be built on chains alone and encouraged the migration of \"Free Settlers\" who chose to come. These farmers, tradesmen, and entrepreneurs arrived with capital and ambition, looking to escape the class rigidity of Britain. They brought the \"Choice\" element that the Convict lacked.",
