      "description": "The Australian government refused to forward the petition to London. Cooper, aged 76, had spent years walking Melbourne streets to gather signatures for citizenship, land rights, and Aboriginal representation in Parliament. William Cooper organized the first Aboriginal political movement, walking the streets of Melbourne to gather 2,000 signatures for a petition to the King demanding citizenship rights. The petition was rejected by the Australian government, but Cooper's act established the Indigenous voice as a continuous challenge to the legitimacy of the colonial state. The \"Cause of the Cause\" is the Prior Claim.",
