      "description": "Barton had spent a decade persuading six jealous colonies to merge into one Commonwealth, driven more by the practicalities of tariffs and rail gauges than revolutionary fervor. The six colonies (NSW, Victoria, Queensland, SA, WA, Tasmania) agreed to merge into a single Commonwealth while retaining significant state powers. It was less a \"Union or Die\" moment than a \"Union for Convenience\" moment, driven by railways and tariffs more than ideology.",
