      "description": "Three days later, on December 3rd, colonial troops stormed the stockade in a 20-minute battle that killed 27 miners and 6 soldiers; Lalor lost his arm but later became Speaker of the Victorian Parliament. The Eureka Stockade rebellion was the only armed uprising in Australian history, where gold miners fought (and lost) against colonial soldiers over the issue of taxation without representation. It lasted 20 minutes, but its memory has persisted for 170 years as the \"Birthplace of Australian Democracy.\"",
