      "source": "Report to the Colonial Office, after his pastoral visit to Norfolk Island, 1846",
      "description": "Willson documented systematic brutality—men flogged until bone showed, forced labor until death—that shocked even Victorian sensibilities and eventually led to the closure of the Second Settlement in 1855. Norfolk Island was the place where the \"incorrigibles\" were sent—the prisoners too dangerous for the mainland. It was a place of systematic torture, designed to break the spirit through labor and the lash. What happened there is the darkest chapter of the convict system.",
