      "description": "Blainey's seminal work explained how 12,000 miles and three months by sail from Britain shaped everything—economy, psychology, and the peculiar mix of isolation and dependence that defines the national character. Blainey's seminal work explained that Australia's isolation from Europe—12,000 miles and three months by sail—was not a trivia point but the dominant force shaping its economy, psychology, and culture. We were far from markets, far from culture, far from \"Home.\"",
